WEBVTT

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.810
Run at once towards a dream

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.810
yume no mukou e ikkini hashitte yo

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.780
Let’s meet and laugh away yesterday’s troubles

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.780
nayameru kinou wo fungiri warai aou

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.860
When our memories were here,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.860
omoide ga itta no toki mo

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.060
even though we are deeply hurt, go straight on

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.060
kizu wo fukai no ni massugu mae ni

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.650
GO TO NEW WORLD

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.470
I can feel it in the wind

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.470
kaze no naka kanjiteru yo

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.130
The hot beat is shining

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.130
atsui kodou kagayaku yo

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.610
especially now…

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.610
ima koso

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.550
surely, always, you’ll be by my side

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.550
kitto zutto soba ni iru yo ne

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.410
Keep on running the way to the future.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.410
mirai no michi wo hashiri tsuzukeyou

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.300
more and more, no matter what happens

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.300
motto motto nani ga okitemo

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.510
half our tears become double smiles

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.510
namida wa hanbun nibai no egao ni naru

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.060
forever

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.060
itsudemo

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.030
That was…

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.530
my deceased mother’s…

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.730
hometown.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.180
First down!

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:53.380
Second down!

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:03.180
Futagozuka means Twin Mound.
You might remember it from Futakoi Original.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.380
I’ve only been to Futagozuka village once.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.180
Ten years ago.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.930
It was at the time of my mother’s funeral.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.230
It’s really rustic.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.480
<i>Really</i> rustic.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.430
Sorry about that.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.830
My mother divorced my dad right after she gave birth to me.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.530
Even if she was my mother,

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:34.630
I had never even met her.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.130
During the funeral as well,

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.980
I didn’t even know what sort of expression to make.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.430
Are you crying?

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:55.240
No.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.610
Are you crying?

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.330
No.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.030
However,

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.630
seeing my dad cry for the first time

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.530
was more of a shock.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.030
I remember it well.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.440
Oh…

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:40.630
He’s here!

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:05.330
It really is very rustic.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.680
Very…

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.330
Sorry about that.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.280
Well then…

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:14.080
This is our goal.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.380
Beauty and comfort!

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.430
Hot springs! Hot springs!

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:23.180
By the way…

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.130
Earlier,

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:25.780
didn’t you two say something like,

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.330
“Even if we don’t go on a trip, just strolling along together is enough?”

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:29.870
I’m pretty sure…

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:32.780
Well,

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:37.380
just being able to go to the hot springs and eat and drink there is a rare opportunity, after all.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:42.980
But for them to be greeting us, even though we have no connection to them…

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.680
they’ve got to be shifty people.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.130
Honestly speaking…

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:51.140
somehow I sense an air of
danger around here.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.140
Oh?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.180
See,

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.080
since long ago there wasn’t anything…

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.780
My head hurts…

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:55.040
Rentarou-chan!!!

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:16.780
Long time no see!

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:17.130
You seem like you’ve grown lots!

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:19.020
You’re so manly now.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:19.020
How long has it been? Ten years?

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:22.130
Hey, hey!

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.130
Was it unexpected? You must be tired.

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:24.930
That’s it, it’s not that you haven’t been.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.820
I meant in this village.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:27.660
Oh come on, everyone’s been…

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.660
We’ve wanted you to come to this village for ages.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:33.530
… to the hot springs at least once.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.990
We were scared to contact you,

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.530
so we sent you the pamphlet.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.280
Ah, why don’t you enter the hot spring!

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.580
Oh! Isn’t that a good idea?

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.950
Hot springs! Hot springs!

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:45.680
So,

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:46.780
who are you,

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:48.380
and where are you from?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.180
Geez, don’t joke around Rentarou-chan!

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:52.380
It’s Kaoruko and…

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.180
…Sumireko!

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.080
Kaoruko-san and…

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:57.380
Sumireko-san?

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:58.080
Yes!

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:07.400
Back then at my mother’s funeral…

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.780
There was a pair of crying twins

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.780
and although I didn’t know them,

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.410
I thought that I should say something.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.480
Out of the blue…

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:20.080
I’ll make you my brides,

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.670
so don’t cry anymore.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.180
In other words,

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:30.050
the wedding ceremony is tomorrow!

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:30.930
Huh?

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:35.630
Is he funny in the head?!

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.680
Well, well, Sara-chan.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.380
Even if they say that
it’s a wedding ceremony,

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:40.880
it’s only a show.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.130
It’s written that

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:45.900
if the twin shrine maidens don’t marry at the Futagozuka shrine…

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.480
Nikogami means “Twin god.”

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.480
it will suffer the curse of the Nikogami.

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:51.430
But,

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:54.180
the Ichijou twins are also having a hard time.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.230
Yup, yup.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:58.780
But you know,

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.780
he suddenly said, “I’ll  make you my brides, so don’t cry anymore.”

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.680
Should we say that Rentarou is cute,

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:06.980
or that he’s silly…

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.430
Even if it’s just a show,

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.680
I still don’t like it.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.560
You haven’t forgotten the reason we came here, have you?

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:24.400
We don’t have much time!

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:27.130
I know.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:32.630
I know that, Sara-chan.

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.630
My apologies for coming at a time like this…

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:07.180
Thanks for everything, Rentarou-san.

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:08.430
That’s right!

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.580
I’ll get you Yumi-chan’s personal effects!

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.080
Oh, no, no, no, no, no!

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.720
I really don’t need those kinds of things.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.330
All these souvenirs

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:18.620
are already enough.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.330
No, no, don’t say that!

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:36.880
Huh? Where is Yumi-chan’s stuff?

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:47.330
What am I gonna do with all this?

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:51.630
Shall we sell these vegetables at the agency?

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:54.880
What’s the matter?

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:57.930
Can it be that you’re angry about the wedding ceremony?

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:01.030
It can’t be helped.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.630
These country people

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:06.730
are really persistent about their customs and rituals, you know?

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:10.330
You should be relieved that it’s only a fake one.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.580
It’s only polite to go along with it, right?

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:14.330
Right?

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.030
Geez,

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:21.680
we’ll finish up quickly.

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:22.880
So while we’re at it,

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.140
you two could take your time at the hot springs or something.

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:28.680
Hmm?

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.880
What’s the matter?

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:32.080
What?

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.980
Do as you please.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.530
I don’t understand you two.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:42.030
It’s the curse.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.830
It’s the curse of Futagozuka!

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:47.580
Stay tuned!

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:05.880
But, what’s the matter
with my set of twins?

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:12.230
I just don’t understand adolescent girls.

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:13.180
Really.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:14.810
Huh?

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:18.730
Yo!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:19.630
Good morn-- oh!

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:38.480
I-Isn’t it nice weather?

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:46.330
Th-This was a mixed bath, right?

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:53.270
I’ll get out first.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:23.580
Rentarou…

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.680
Let’s be together forever…

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.130
Looks like there’s someone in there.

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:37.820
H-Hey, there are people…!

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:21.680
I don’t understand this…

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:39.180
Oh, Sendaido,

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:41.680
thank you very much for everything.

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:42.760
Not at all.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.230
What’s the matter, Kanushi-san?

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:47.530
Well,

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:50.580
I haven’t seen Kaoruko and Sumireko anywhere.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:51.930
Do you know where they are?

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.030
No,

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:55.060
where could they have gone?

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:07.530
Umm…

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:08.630
Shirogane-san?

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:19.580
I’m sorry.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:20.530
Huh?

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.580
Even if they say it’s only a show,

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:26.780
your boyfriend going through a
wedding ceremony with other girls

00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.380
would make you unhappy, right?

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.730
It was a long time ago…

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:31.670
and since he had made a promise like that back then…

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:37.130
We thought it would be fun to call Rentarou-chan…

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:40.780
We didn’t even think that he’d already have such cute girlfriends.

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:42.980
I’m really sorry.

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:44.690
I’m sorry.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:50.230
You know,

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:53.080
we were thinking of
not doing the ceremony.

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:54.280
What?

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:56.280
You can’t do that!

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.280
We don’t care.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:02.130
It’s not like anyone in the village actually believes in the curse of the Nikogami anyway.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:03.630
It’s all just acting, you know?

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:06.930
There’ll also be people from the media.

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:08.730
If we just appear in front of the altar,

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:09.980
it’ll be perfectly okay.

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:13.900
We’ll just perform the service as always, or something like that.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:14.730
Yes!

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:17.130
It’s all right, it’s all right!

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:18.250
That’s why, sorry.

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.480
You aren’t the ones at fault.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.400
It’s our problem.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:32.730
Time…

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:34.330
There’s no time, so we’re in a hurry.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:35.530
Sara-chan!

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:36.680
That story…

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.480
Our 16th birthday is coming soon.

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:42.030
Then,

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:46.210
we can’t be together.

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:48.380
You can’t be together…

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.210
with Soujyu-san?

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:53.960
With Rentarou-chan?

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:00.930
That’s why…

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.630
I thought if we became one…

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:31.580
I’d like to speak with you immediately.

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:47.330
Sara and Soujyu have
both returned to Tokyo.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:50.680
I don’t know what happened…

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:52.930
But,

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:54.430
they must be really angry about something.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:56.750
That was the premonition that I had.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:27.680
Where did he go, my son-in-law?

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.320
Rentarou-chan, hang in there!

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:58.380
Eternal Love.  Ainosuke

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.380
Are you crying?

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:03.880
No.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:06.780
Are you crying?

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:08.580
No.

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:12.930
Why did you separate, even though you love each other?

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.880
Why, I wonder…

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:19.230
That day,

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:21.130
when he said that,

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.430
my dad quietly lowered the brim of his hat.

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:28.530
And then,

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:29.870
I remember Sara and Soujyu.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:34.630
I remember the two years that we’ve spent together:

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:36.960
The carefree days…

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:42.050
Those times when we ran while excitedly chasing a UFO…

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:46.530
Walking and carrying a bucket, the atmosphere at the riverbank…

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:51.680
The bitterness of the coal-black burnt “Hot Cake”…

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:57.280
In a way, the sheer number of those memories at that moment

00:20:57.280 --> 00:20:59.700
wouldn’t stop burning inside my chest.

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:28.980
Sara? Where are you?

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:30.980
Sorry.

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:31.780
Where?

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:32.560
Where are you?

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:48.950
Rentarou…

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:55.880
I don’t understand this.

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:06.630
I don’t understand this.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:12.780
Say…

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:15.080
Shall we continue on from the hot springs?

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:25.800
We are here.

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:25.630
bokura wa koko ni iru

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:33.200
We will be here.

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:33.200
bokura ga koko ni aru

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:38.520
The slow time is

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:38.520
yuruyaka na jikan ga

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:45.450
flowing in this room.

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:45.450
nagareteru kono heya de

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:49.050
Even if the summer days vanish,

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:49.050
natsu no hi ga kiete mo

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:53.110
the smiles that remain

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:53.110
nokoru egao tachi

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:59.990
are a chain of happiness up to this point.

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:59.990
kocchi made shiawase no rensa

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:05.830
Ah, the meaning of honesty,

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:05.830
aa sunaosa no imi

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:14.170
is within the innermost depths of your heart.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:14.170
KOKORO no zutto zutto oku no hou e

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:19.550
Hey, the days are wonderful

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:19.550
nee subarashii hibi

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:27.310
in the midst of weakness and anxiety.

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:27.310
yowasa to fuan no naka de shitte

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:33.860
I won’t say goodbye, Because forever

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:33.860
sayonara wa iwanai yo datte itsumademo

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:39.140
the days will be unchanged.

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:39.140
kawaru koto no nai hibi

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:45.980
Surely forever. M

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:45.980
kitto itsumademo

